  "cause": "**The war has stopped being fought for a decision and started being kept at a temperature, and the Gulf states are discovering they are inside the thermostat.** On Tuesday **Iran's Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps** said it fired **six drones** at the US air-defence radar facility at **al-Riffa air base in Bahrain** — the **third** Iranian drone attack on Bahrain in **five days**, after a lull of several weeks, with sirens sounding across **Manama**. Bahrain's military said its air defences intercepted the attack *\"before they could achieve their objectives\"*; the foreign ministry said the kingdom *\"condemns in the strongest terms the continued brutal Iranian attacks on its territory and holds Iran fully responsible for their consequences.\"* The same night **Kuwait's armed forces** reported the country *\"under attack by drones\"* and told the public that *\"any explosion sounds heard are the result of air defence systems intercepting hostile attacks.\"* The US struck **Qeshm Island** in the Strait of Hormuz — Iran's deputy governor for Hormozgan, **Ahmad Nafisi**, told IRNA that five or six explosions were heard but that the strikes caused *\"no damage to residential, commercial, or infrastructural areas\"*; a US official told Al Jazeera the target was a **missile launch site**, in response to the Bahrain attack. The IRGC's own statement was not diplomatic: *\"The Strait of Hormuz is closed, and any aggression by the American enemy will be met with an even harsher and more forceful response.\"* **The maritime layer is now a permanent hazard rather than an incident.** Iran's armed forces said **three oil tankers** struck naval mines while attempting to cross the strait on Tuesday; the UK Maritime Trade Operations agency separately reported two tanker attacks on Monday, including the Panamanian-flagged **Tara Gas**, disabled with an engine-room fire seven nautical miles north of **Khasab, Oman**. In northern Iraq a drone over the **Khor Mor** gas field triggered sirens — production there had already been halted the previous week after a suspected drone attack that cut **2.8 gigawatts** of generation. And the human bill is being litigated: a **14-page whistleblower complaint** obtained by Al Jazeera alleges that the army was warned *\"at least three times in the week before hostilities\"* that the **Port of Shuaiba** in Kuwait was vulnerable, that the fortified site had **no roof, no physician, no fixed aid station and one ambulance**, and that at least one of the **six service members** killed — the deadliest single assault on US forces since the war began — *\"could have survived.\"* More than **23** American service members have been killed in the war. Defense Secretary **Pete Hegseth** had described the drone as a *\"squirter\"* that *\"happened to hit a tactical operations centre that was fortified.\"* **And the diplomatic track has been deliberately emptied.** **Trump** said last week the war was *\"militarily … effectively over\"* while adding he *\"would not hesitate\"* to resume strikes; this week he said the US was **no longer interested in a deal** and directed Vice-President **JD Vance** — who had been running the negotiation and who blamed the party's **3 November** midterm losses on the war and fuel prices — to focus on domestic politics. Iran's president **Masoud Pezeshkian** said Supreme Leader **Mojtaba Khamenei** had ordered an end to the state of *\"neither war nor peace\"*, and parliament speaker **Mohammad Bagher Ghalibaf**, the chief negotiator, told Al Jazeera that *\"the ball is now in the American court.\"* Meanwhile the **IAEA** reported it is *\"increasingly concerned\"* about a uranium enrichment plant at **Isfahan** it has never been allowed to visit — announced by Iran on **12 June 2025**, a day before Israel's strikes began — and that it does not know the facility's location or whether it holds nuclear material: *\"a matter of serious proliferation concern… and needs to be rectified with the utmost urgency.\"* Before the June 2025 strikes Iran held an estimated **441 kg** of uranium enriched to **60 per cent**.",
