  "verse": "And know that whatever you do which is unright, it will come back on you; and battle (war) also belongs to unright and great terribleness and you shall avoid it with all good and fair (responsible) means as well as with love; only peace and freedom, love and consonance (harmony) amongst all peoples of your kind (humankind) is the way of equitableness (fairness) and of the truth of the laws and recommendations of the primal power (Creation); consider, battle (war) is never a way to the creation of peace, freedom, love and consonance (harmony), but only a way of mishappening, hatred, unpeace, unfreedom (bondage), dissonance (disharmony), pillage, revenge and retaliation, robbery, destruction and boundless outrage with bloody deeds (killing) and defilement (violation).",
  "verseSrc": "Chapter 8, Verse 42",
  "hinge": "§8:42 makes a claim that reads as moral and is in fact structural: war is *\"never a way to the creation of peace\"* — not because peace is nicer, but because war generates the specific conditions (hatred, bondage, retaliation, destruction) that make peace impossible to build on. A frozen conflict is the empirical proof. Both parties have now discovered that the unresolved state is survivable and that resolving it is expensive: Washington keeps a blockade that costs it readiness and buys it nothing; Tehran keeps a closed strait that costs it revenue and buys it leverage; the Gulf keeps absorbing drones. The verse's instruction is not pacifism — it explicitly permits defence in extremis — it is that the *cause* must be changed rather than managed. Three moves would change it. **First, publish the rules of passage** — a notified corridor, a published inspection regime, and a named authority for both, because *\"the Strait of Hormuz is closed\"* is a claim, and a waterway governed by competing claims is governed by whoever is willing to shoot; a corridor with published rules converts a military contest into an administrative one, which is the only form of contest Iran and the US can both lose gracefully. **Second, release the Shuaiba investigation** — the completed report, the three warnings, and the structural finding, because a military that withholds the finding will re-buy the lesson at the next unroofed outpost, and the families have already paid for the document. **Third, get inspectors into Isfahan or say publicly that you cannot** — an announced inability is a policy allies can plan around; an unannounced one is a surprise waiting for a bad week. The war is being managed because management is what the calendar rewards. §8:42 says plainly what management produces."
