  "cause": "**COP31 enters its final days with the central question still bracketed, and the target that defined a decade of climate diplomacy has quietly lost its name.** The conference in **Antalya** concludes on **Friday, 20 November**. Ministers have arrived to negotiate the **cover decision** — the single text that summarises what the parties agree — after Monday's first draft carried **two competing formulations** on fossil fuels and flagged divergence on the electrification target and on adaptation finance. The New York Times' assessment this week is blunt: the slogan **\"Keep 1.5 Alive\"** is dead, as the world blows past the threshold it named. UN News' summary of Tuesday's session is equally direct: *\"'Standing up' is the easy part. Reaching agreement is proving considerably harder,\"* with ministers *\"struggling to bridge divisions over fossil fuels and climate finance.\"* **What is in the draft is instructive: the ocean, and not the source of the power.** The first draft contains prominent provisions on **oceans**, reflecting a push by co-hosts **Australia and Türkiye**; a study presented at the summit found that more than **95 per cent** of coastal and island nations now include ocean-related measures in their national climate plans, while around **60 per cent** of those commitments depend on additional finance or technical support. **Marine Lecerf** of the Ocean and Climate Platform told journalists: *\"We're not asking for a new mandate, we're asking for acceleration.\"* On the **35-by-35** electrification pledge — raising electricity's share of final energy consumption from roughly 23 to 35 per cent by 2035 — the count of signatories has not materially moved from the roughly **thirty** recorded at the presidency's mid-point press conference, and the **Like-Minded Developing Countries** bloc, including **China, India and Bangladesh**, has said it will not endorse an electrification pledge in the final text. The **United States** remains outside the process. The summit runs more than **160 agenda items** to a Friday deadline.",
  "bullets": [
   "**A cover decision that names what is easy and brackets what is causal is a document about the wrong thing** — ocean provisions in the draft, two phrasings on fossil fuels, adaptation finance still open; the direct effect is that Friday produces a text with real content about the sea and no enforceable content about the cause; the compound consequence is that the ocean clauses become the evidence the process works, cited for a decade, while the sentence that would have changed the energy mix remains in brackets — the instrument and the alibi written in the same document",
   "**Retiring \"1.5\" without replacing it with a mechanism removes the only unit of account the negotiations had** — a target abandoned by exhaustion rather than by decision; the direct effect is that every national plan is now measured against nothing; the compound consequence is that without a shared denominator ambition becomes a matter of national self-description, and the ratchet at the heart of the Paris architecture loses its reference point — which is not a softening of the policy but the removal of the instrument",
   "**A pledge that thirty countries sign and the largest emitters decline is a coalition, and coalitions do not bind successors** — 35 by 35, no \"clean\" qualifier, the LMDC refusing the text, the US absent, China hedging; the direct effect is that the final decision will *note* the initiative rather than adopt it; the compound consequence is that the countries that did sign have accepted a target whose achievement will be credited to them and whose failure will be shared with everyone — a distribution of accountability that guarantees nobody defends it in 2035",
   "**Finance is the actual negotiating text, and it is being deferred behind the language fight** — around 60 per cent of existing ocean commitments conditional on support, adaptation finance open, ministers arriving to bridge exactly this; the direct effect is that the headline fight over \"fossil fuels\" consumes the political oxygen; the compound consequence is that the adaptation gap is settled by default at whatever the cover decision does not say, and the countries that need the money are the ones whose commitments are already conditional on it",
   "**A conference concluding four days after a trilateral of the three largest military powers will be read through that trilateral** — Antalya closing Friday, Shenzhen meeting Thursday, the US absent from both the room and the text; the direct effect is that climate's political weight is measured against a war summit; the compound consequence is that the process is progressively priced as a humanitarian sideline, which is precisely the framing that lets governments fund reconstruction and rearmament from the same fiscal space they decline to spend on mitigation"
  ],
  "verse": "See that your deeds are not the same as ashes which the wind blows on a stormy day and casts them to all the winds (all points of the compass). See that your deeds are long-lasting, just as if you are building a house on a rock with its foundations set into the rock.",
  "verseSrc": "Goblet of the Truth",
  "hinge": "§14:11–12 draws the distinction that the cover decision is failing: between a deed and ashes, and between a deed and a foundation. A pledge is not a deed. A pledge signed by thirty countries, with no qualifier on the source of the electricity, no funding attached to the commitments that depend on it, and a target that the largest emitters have declined to endorse, is precisely the thing the verse describes — an announcement cast to all points of the compass on a stormy day. The hinge is not more ambition; it is **building the two clauses that would make Friday's text structural**. **First,** pair the electrification target with its source in a single operative paragraph, so that no delegation can vote for the growth number while reserving its position on generation — the Like-Minded bloc's objection is to an instrument whose meaning it cannot control, which is a legitimate objection to a badly written pledge. **Second,** attach a **conditional-finance schedule** to the ocean and adaptation commitments — the roughly 60 per cent that depend on support should be listed with an amount, a donor and a date, because a commitment conditional on money that is never named is a commitment that has already been withdrawn. **Third,** and this is the one that determines whether 2035 exists as a policy: say in the cover decision what replaces 1.5 as the reference point — cumulative emissions, a carbon budget, or a stated overshoot with a return date. A number retired in silence is not realism. It is the removal of the measuring instrument and the announcement that measurement has ended."
